## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [NEW] `backend/app/__init__.py`
Flask app factory with CORS, blueprint registration, and error handlers.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/config.py`
Configuration class loading `DATABASE_URL`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `UPLOAD_FOLDER` from environment variables.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/extensions.py`
SQLAlchemy, Flask-Migrate, and Flask-CORS initialization.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/models/*.py`
5 SQLAlchemy models matching the database schema above. Employee has a unique constraint on `ippis_number`. Payslip has a composite unique on `(employee_id, month_year)`.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/services/excel_parser.py`
Reads the uploaded Excel file using `openpyxl`. Creates/updates Employee records. Handles the header row (row 2) and data rows (row 3+).

#### [NEW] `backend/app/services/pdf_parser.py`
Parses each page of the payslip PDF using `pdfplumber`. Extracts employee info, earnings, deductions, and summary totals. Matches to Employee records via IPPIS number. Runs as a background thread to avoid request timeouts.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/services/ai_service.py`
Takes a natural language query, sends it to Gemini API with the database schema as context, receives a structured filter object back, and executes it against the database.

#### [NEW] `backend/app/routes/*.py`
6 route blueprints implementing the 14 API endpoints listed above.

#### [NEW] `backend/requirements.txt`
```
flask
flask-sqlalchemy
flask-migrate
flask-cors
psycopg2-binary
openpyxl
pdfplumber
gunicorn
